    },
    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how many pizza slices each of Henry and his friends can have if they share the pizzas equally, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pizza slices.\n2. Determine how many slices each person will get by dividing the total number of slices by the number of people.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of pizza slices. Since each pizza is cut into 8 slices and there are 7 pizzas, we multiply the number of pizzas by the number of slices per pizza:\n\\[ 7 \\text{ pizzas} \\times 8 \\text{ slices per pizza} = 56 \\text{ slices} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many slices each person will get. There are 4 people in total (Henry and his 3 friends), so we divide the total number of slices by the number of people:\n\\[ 56 \\text{ slices} \\div 4 \\text{ people} = 14 \\text{ slices per person} \\]\n\nTherefore, each person can have \\(\\boxed{14}\\) slices.",
